params.prompt:
Write a narrated short video script for children.
Title: {{subject.title}}
Learning goal: {{subject.learning_goal}}
Hook: {{subject.hook}}
Tone: {{subject.tone}}
Total narration about {{words_target}} words across {{scene_count}} scenes. Each scene: one or two short spoken sentences and a vivid visual description. Open with the hook in the first sentence. End with a friendly call to subscribe.

Global art style: {{style}}. Keep characters and palette consistent.
For each scene visual below, write a detailed image-generation prompt and a very short on-screen caption (max 8 words).
Scenes: {{scene_descriptions}}

Create {{platform}} SEO metadata for a kids short video.
Working title: {{title}}
Summary: {{summary}}
Seed keywords: {{keyword_seed}}
Rules (2026 Shorts best practice): the primary search keyword MUST be in the first 40 characters of the title; title under 70 chars, curiosity-driven, max 1 emoji, no false clickbait. Description: a strong 1-line hook, a 3-5 sentence keyword-rich summary, then exactly 3-5 niche hashtags plus #Shorts (never more than 5 total hashtags). Provide {{max_tags}} lowercase search tags. hashtags list: the same 3-5 niche tags plus #Shorts, each starting with #. Strictly family-safe.

Audience: {{audience}}. Review this content for safety, age-appropriateness and brand risk.
Title: {{title}}
Script: {{script}}
Reject anything scary, violent, sexual, hateful, unsafe, deceptive, or impersonating real brands/people. Respond strictly as JSON.
